 own cells. Bioartificial organs might change transplanting forever.  Scientists are already growing noses, ears and blood vessels. Lab-grown bladders are also successful.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le05ob10re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "40000", "text": "<p>Other engineered organs are in the pipeline. Wouldn't everyone wish they could have the new organ they needed, produced from their own cells? Soon this may become commonplace.</p><p>Biological structures made with 3D technology from digital files may soon be accessible. Wish you could be on the cutting edge of this new technology?</p>This may become the fastest growing field in the future. You could start with a 3D printing course at college, online, or even at your local library.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le05ob10re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le05ob10re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0}]}